---
import Policy, { type Outline } from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import Row from '../components/Row.astro';
import { COMPANY, SITE } from '../data/site';

// How Zaaheen uses AI (founder, session 67; both research reports: "AI & Data
// page, recommended", and no peer has one). Facts checked in session 67: the
// search model ships in the installer, the ranking and tidying models are
// downloaded (vault-app model_fetch.rs, vault-llm phi4_mini.rs), the read path
// has no language model (the architectural lock: the vault returns facts, the
// agent composes), and tidying is off until switched on. White label: no model
// or vendor names here, only what each one does.
const OUTLINE: Outline[] = [
  { id: 'models', title: 'The AI inside Zaaheen', topics: [
    { id: 'what', title: 'What the AI in Zaaheen does' },
    { id: 'where', title: 'Where it runs' },
    { id: 'answers', title: 'Zaaheen finds facts, your AI app answers' },
  ] },
  { id: 'tidying', title: 'Tidying up', topics: [
    { id: 'how-tidying', title: 'What tidying changes' },
    { id: 'control', title: 'You decide when it runs' },
  ] },
  { id: 'promises', title: 'Our promises', topics: [
    { id: 'no-training', title: 'Your memories never train AI' },
    { id: 'your-apps', title: 'What your AI apps send to their makers' },
    { id: 'contact', title: 'Questions' },
  ] },
];
const topic = (id: string) =>
  OUTLINE.flatMap((s) => s.topics).find((t) => t.id === id)?.title ?? id;
const lede = `${SITE.name} uses AI to keep your memories easy to find. All of it runs on your own computer. Here is exactly what it does, and what it never does.`;
---
<Policy path="/ai-and-your-data/" heading="AI and Your Data" lede={lede} outline={OUTLINE}>
  <ul slot="summary">
    <li>Zaaheen's AI runs on your computer. Your memories are never sent to an online AI
        service by Zaaheen.</li>
    <li>It finds the right memories for your AI apps. It doesn't chat with you or write
        answers.</li>
    <li>Tidying up is off until you turn it on, and it never deletes a memory.</li>
    <li>Your memories are never used to train AI, by us or for anyone else.</li>
  </ul>

  <section id="models" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">The AI inside Zaaheen</h2>

    <Row id="what" title={topic('what')} where="Three small models">
      <p>Zaaheen uses three small AI models, each with one job:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Understanding meaning</strong>, so a search for "my coffee order" also finds
            "I drink flat whites". It comes with the app.</li>
        <li><strong>Ranking results</strong>, so the most relevant memories come first. The app
            downloads it the first time it starts.</li>
        <li><strong>Tidying up</strong>, which merges duplicates and settles contradictions. The
            app downloads it only when you turn tidying on, about 2.5 GB, once.</li>
      </ul>
    </Row>

    <Row id="where" title={topic('where')} where="On your computer">
      <p>All three run on your own computer, using its processor. Once downloaded, they work
         offline, and your memories never pass through an online AI service on the way. That is
         why Zaaheen can promise that we never see your memories: there is no server in the
         middle to see them.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="answers" title={topic('answers')} where="Your AI apps">
      <p>When an AI app such as Claude or ChatGPT asks Zaaheen a question, Zaaheen hands back the
         memories that match, as they are stored. It doesn't make up an answer or
         talk to you. The AI app you are using writes the reply, using those facts.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>

  <section id="tidying" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">Tidying up</h2>

    <Row id="how-tidying" title={topic('how-tidying')} where="Consolidation">
      <p>Tidying up merges near-duplicates into one memory, settles facts that contradict each
         other in favour of the newer one, and moves memories you never use out of everyday
         recall. It also writes short summaries of each topic and adds other ways of phrasing a
         memory, so your AI apps find it whatever words they use.</p>
      <p>It works only from what you have saved and never deletes a memory. Like any AI, it can
         occasionally get something wrong, so check anything important before relying on it.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="control" title={topic('control')} where="Settings">
      <p>Tidying is off unless you switch on <em>Keep my vault tidy automatically</em>. You choose
         every day or once a week and the time, or run it yourself whenever you like. You can
         turn it off again at any time.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>

  <section id="promises" class="docs-section">
    <h2 class="docs-title">Our promises</h2>

    <Row id="no-training" title={topic('no-training')} where="Always">
      <p>We never use your memories to train AI models, and we never give them to anyone who
         would. We couldn't even if we wanted to: they never reach us.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="your-apps" title={topic('your-apps')} where="Your choice">
      <p>The AI apps you connect are made by other companies. When one uses a memory to answer
         you, it may send that memory to its maker's servers as part of your conversation. What
         happens next, including whether your conversations train their models, depends on that
         company's policy and your settings with them. You choose which apps to connect, and you
         can remove Zaaheen from any of them at any time.</p>
      <p>More about what we handle is in our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </Row>

    <Row id="contact" title={topic('contact')} where="Email">
      <p>Questions about how Zaaheen uses AI: <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>.</p>
    </Row>
  </section>
</Policy>
